Mon/Hum/Mal/Neu

Man, this one was a real roller coaster of near-death experiences and
awesome luck. That is if at the very start the coaster soars up so high
and then plummeted during the entire game right up untill the astral
plane.

This had been my most behaved ascension so far in my goal of ascending
all classes. My Monk was a strict vegan, never hit with a wielded
weapon, never polymorphed an object, never changed form and never
wished for an artifact. With a character that gains so little hp and
has very limited AC, the pilypiling one was sorrowly missed.

Sledge began his journey with a successful protection racket, gaining 8
points of protection from the minetown priest at Xp:1. Combined with a
magic lamp found on level 1 and an armour store on level 2 I was happy
as a clam. That unfortunatly, was the end of any good luck i'd recieve.

By the time I was finished all that I was a Xp:1 monk with an angry
god, and the minetown altar was chaotic. So I started gaining levels
like crazy and headed down in search of an altar. level 2...no, level
3...no, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9..Neutral temple! Finally! (the bad luck of
having to go so deep outweighs the fact of it being a temple in my
mind). I appease my god and I go on my merry way solving sokoban
(amulet) and the mines.

Eventually im back at the temple with nowhere to go but down. But wait!
Lucky me! I have no magic resistance or a bag of holding let alone a
sack! >_>   (this is the first time ive gone this far without those). I
still had my magic lamp, and lets just say after many near-death
experiances in diving down in search for a CoMR I give up and wish it
up.

I save the quest for later given what ive hear about the monk quest
nemisis being the toughest. I make it to the castle and lo and behold
the WoW is 0:1. Wish 1, 2 charging scrolls (ended up with 1), charge,
wish 2 helm of brilliance, wish 3 speed boots, wish 4 bag of
holding(not one was randomly found in the dungeons). I saved the last
one for another time.

I enter the quest armed with my fists and a spell of sleep. I made my
way to Master Kaens level. He got 1 hit on my that took 25 of my 125
hp. I put him to sleep and beat em to death in about 5 turns. If I
didnt have that sleep spell I dont think id stand a chance.

Eyes of the overworld take over the orb of fate's spot of most awesome
artifact in my book. Hell wouldve actually been fun if it wasnt for my
wimpy AC going up against minotaurs (genocided them, were brutal
without dragon scale mail) and losing half of the named demons.

I make it to the bottom level, mark the square and began to arrange my
kit asap. I've had enough with this monk.

Just before I headed to Rodneys tower for a cup of coffee I decided to
use my last with for a pet archon. I knew the sanctum and endgames
would be brutal with my AC so I thought a sidekick would help. I wished
up the figurine, and enclosed mycelf in a locked room away from
everything incase things go bad. Lo and behold my luck again, I now
have a peeved off archon breathing down my neck. I teleported out of
there right away and started writing up some taming scrolls to try and
salvage my mistake. In doing so I made yet another mistake in  thinking
I could tame someing much high leveled then me with taming scrolls.
Idiot. So I wasted more of my markers charges but luckly I never needed
them again. I decide it was best to keep the archon locked up instead
of trying to kill it.

I begin the ascension and killed Rodney. I enter the sanctum and it is
there that I almost lost hope. My AC was poorer then I imagined.
Countless times the priests were bringing me down to dangerously low hp
levels. Elbereth combined with a fort of summoned insects really saved
my butt. When my hp and energy regenerated I battled my way into the
temple and locked the door. Hello high priest, say hello to my WoDeath.
After I got the amulet and #(n)amed it I spent many turns gaining back
my energy. Rodney never showed up in there. When I was ready and I saw
all the priests were far away from me I headed out and teleported
myself a nice little path. I was amazed that I got out of there alive
when I climbed up those stairs.

Teleport, teleport teleport, ah! Rodney! "Rodney drinks a potion of
gain level, Rodney rises up through the ceiling", sucker.

Plane of earth was no trouble. Plane of air was easier then I expected.
No archons were generated there, them being the source of my barbarians
demise some while ago. I was surprised how well my AC held up against
the air elementals. Fire was a little worrying. The portal was on the
far side and durring the entire sprint towards it I had an army of fire
monster lead by an archon chasing me. Thank you speed boots. Water was
no trouble, I had water monsters genocided.

Finally I had some luck in the astral plane. I arrived on the left
side, which had pestilence. Armed with my wand of death I charged
through there teleport rays flying. Pesty down in one blast. Teleported
my way to the temple which was mine, and the rest is history.


